Phase 0 audit confirmed the orchestrator's "shim" was products/adconnect/backend/app/auth_deps.py — a legitimate custom-JWT auth realm (NOT in seed/), used by 7 routers, coexisting with the seed's Supabase realm for standard routers. Renaming and "deleting" both ruled out; the actual rationalization target was the adjacent dead-code app/dependencies.py.

Phase 1: deleted app/dependencies.py (zero importers; create_product_app builds its own deps internally; eliminated 422-trap surface for ProductDependencies.get_org_id/get_user_role/get_user_client). Expanded app/auth_deps.py docstring to document the two-realm split + N=1 carve-out from canonical Supabase factories + AdConnect MVP Phase 1 forward compat.

Phase 2: 10 direct unit tests for get_current_user + require_role (no token / invalid / wrong role / valid / multi-allowed). Status-code-assertion rule applied. **Surfaced + fixed a latent bug**: app/security.py referenced settings.jwt_expires_minutes which didn't exist on SeedSettings — POST /auth/login and POST /auth/register would have raised AttributeError on first distributor login. Added field with default 60 + rationale comment.

Phase 3 / three-way sync: KB § PATTERNS/backend.md gained a Custom-JWT carve-out (AdConnect — N=1) subsection + migration history entry; memory feedback_auth_factory_pattern.md updated; CLAUDE.md pointer unchanged (already aimed at amended section). verify-kb-sync.sh → OK.

Verification:
- products/adconnect/backend tests: 41 passed (was 31; +10).
- seed/framework/backend deprecation tests: 4 passed (no regression).
- KB sync: ✓.

Closes the immediate rationalization. Cross-product rollout (PF/Therapy/ERP/...) remains tracked under predecessor's seed-auth-deps-cross-product-rollout follow-up; AdConnect explicitly NOT part of that rollout (custom-JWT carve-out documented).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
