+### Custom-JWT carve-out (AdConnect — N=1)
+
+The factories above (`make_get_current_user`, `make_get_current_user_org`,
+`make_require_role`) all assume **Supabase as the JWT validator** — their
+inner path calls `admin.auth.get_user(token)`. That fits 9 of the 10
+products. **AdConnect deviates legitimately** — its B2B distributors log in
+with email/password issued by AdConnect, not via Supabase SSO, so
+`products/adconnect/backend/app/auth_deps.py` ships a **custom-JWT realm**
+(HS256 minted by `app/security.create_token` against `app/data/store.users`)
+that **coexists** with the Supabase realm used by the standard routers
+(health/team/notificacoes). The two realms validate disjoint signatures and
+mount on disjoint URL prefixes — no conflict.
+
+**N=1 = no formalization.** Per the recurrence rule, a single deviation stays
+product-local; if a 2nd custom-JWT product appears the absorption target is
+`make_custom_jwt_user(jwt_secret, jwt_algorithm, user_resolver)` factory in
+`noctusai_lib.api.auth`. Until then, AdConnect is the documented carve-out.
+
+**Why this lives in the KB doc:** future agents reading `KB § PATTERNS/backend.md`
+to wire auth on a product / route need to know the canonical pattern HAS a
+deviation. Without this paragraph, an agent encountering AdConnect's
+`auth_deps.py` would (a) think it's a leftover shim and try to delete it, or
+(b) try to "unify" it against the Supabase factories and break the distributor
+login flow. The orchestrator's first-read of the file in 2026-05-10 hit
+exactly that trap — surfaced by `auth-deps-shim-sweep` Phase 0.
+
 ### Migration history
 
 - 2026-05-04: `make_get_current_user_org` shipped to
