@@ -1,10 +1,38 @@
 """
-AdConnect domain authentication dependencies.
+AdConnect domain authentication dependencies — the custom-JWT realm.
 
-AdConnect uses its own JWT-based auth (not Supabase). These dependencies are
-used by the domain routers (products, cart, orders, rewards, sellout, financial,
-distributors, admin). The framework's standard routers (health, team, notificacoes)
-use Supabase auth via dependencies.py — they coexist without conflict.
+AdConnect runs **two auth realms** simultaneously:
+
+1. **Custom-JWT realm (this module).** Domain routers (auth, products, cart,
+   orders, rewards, sellout, financial, distributors, admin) authenticate via
+   HS256 JWT minted by ``app/security.create_token()`` against the in-memory
+   ``app/data/store.users`` (seeded by ``_seed_users()`` in ``app/routers/auth.py``).
+   This realm exists because B2B distributors log in with email/password issued
+   by AdConnect, NOT via Supabase SSO.
+
+2. **Supabase realm (the seed framework).** Standard routers mounted by
+   ``create_product_app(..., standard_routers=["health", "team", "notificacoes"])``
+   use the seed's ``ProductDependencies`` (Supabase-backed). Their tests live in
+   ``tests/integration/test_e2e_flows.py`` (TestAuthBoundary suite).
+
+The two realms coexist without conflict because they mount on disjoint URL
+prefixes and validate disjoint token-issuer signatures (custom HS256 vs.
+Supabase JWT). **Don't unify them** — the realms serve different login flows.
+
+**N=1 across the platform.** No other product has custom-JWT auth; the seed
+factories (``noctusai_lib.api.auth.make_get_current_user`` /
+``make_get_current_user_org`` / ``make_require_role``) all assume Supabase as
+the validator. If a 2nd custom-JWT product ever appears, the recurrence rule
+fires and the pattern formalizes into seed (``make_custom_jwt_user`` factory).
+Until then, AdConnect is the documented carve-out — see
+``KB § PATTERNS/backend.md § Auth — canonical pattern`` for the canonical
+(Supabase) pattern this module deliberately deviates from.
+
+**See also:** ``products/adconnect/projects/adconnect-mvp-implementation/PROJECT.md``
+Phase 1 will decide whether AdConnect migrates to SSO (Option A — this module
+gets deleted) or finalizes custom-JWT (Option B — this module gains a real
+``adconnect.users`` table backing). This module's current shape supports either
+outcome without churning consumers.
 """
 from __future__ import annotations
 
