+# auth-deps-shim-sweep — Project Document
+
+> **This is a living document.** Update phases / change log as you build.
+>
+> **Project slug:** `auth-deps-shim-sweep` — lives at `projects/auth-deps-shim-sweep/` (cross-cutting; touches a product + KB).
+
+- **Created:** 2026-05-10
+- **Last updated:** 2026-05-10
+- **Status:** All phases ✅ — engineer-side close complete; architect FF-merge pending
+- **Owner / stakeholders:** rapha (user) · architect-agent · engineer-agent (this branch)
+- **Related docs:**
+  - `KB § PATTERNS/backend.md § Auth — canonical pattern` (target for any reference / amendment)
+  - `seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/api/auth.py` (canonical `make_get_current_user` / `make_get_current_user_org` / `make_require_role`)
+  - `seed/framework/backend/noctusai_seed/dependencies.py` (deprecated `ProductDependencies` class with frame-aware DeprecationWarning)
+  - `archive/projects/2026-05-06/01-seed-auth-deps-hardening/PROJECT.md` (predecessor — landed factory + deprecation warning)
+  - `products/adconnect/projects/adconnect-mvp-implementation/PROJECT.md` (Phase 6/8 trigger)
+  - `products/adconnect/backend/app/auth_deps.py` (the SHIM — local custom-JWT auth, the actual subject of this sweep)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Context & Purpose
+
+AdConnect MVP Phase 6/8 surfaced a **deprecated-shape `auth_deps` shim** that the orchestrator initially marked for sweeping deletion. Closer examination during the project close determined the shim has GENUINE VALUE — it implements AdConnect's **product-local custom-JWT auth** (NOT the Supabase-based seed auth). The architect re-targeted the project from "delete it" to "rationalize and possibly extend."
+
+**The actual surface** (Phase 0 audit confirmed):
+
+- `products/adconnect/backend/app/auth_deps.py` — 40-line product-local file. Exposes `get_current_user(creds: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials = Depends(_bearer))` + `require_role(*roles)` factory. Validates a HS256 JWT minted by `app/security.create_token()` against the in-memory `data/store.users`. **7 routers depend on it** (financial, admin, rewards, sellout, auth, orders, distributors).
+- `products/adconnect/backend/app/dependencies.py` — 18-line file that re-exports the deprecated `ProductDependencies` Supabase methods (`get_current_user`, `get_user_role`, `get_org_id`, `get_user_client`, `get_admin_client`). **Zero consumers** — every router imports from `..auth_deps`, never from `..dependencies`. **Dead-code trap** — exposes the FastAPI-broken methods (`get_org_id` / `get_user_role` / `get_user_client`) for future code to wire into `Depends(...)` and trigger the 422-query-param bug.
+
+**The win:** the project rationalizes both files — keep `auth_deps.py` as the canonical custom-JWT auth surface (not a "shim", a real product seam), and either delete the dead-code `dependencies.py` or shrink it to the parts AdConnect actually uses (admin-client, core-client, schema setup).
+
+**Why the orchestrator's first read said "delete":** the file is named `auth_deps.py` (legacy filename pattern from before the seed factory existed) and lives alongside a deprecated `dependencies.py`. The architect's re-targeting recognizes that the *file's content* is legitimate (custom JWT, brand+distributor login, role gating) — the *naming* and the *coexistence with a dead-code dependencies.py* are what looked like a shim.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Confirmed constraints
+
+- **AdConnect uses custom JWT, not Supabase auth, for distributor + brand-admin login** — `app/auth.py` POST /auth/login mints a HS256 token via `app/security.create_token`; users live in the in-memory `app/data/store.users` (seeded by `_seed_users()`). The AdConnect MVP project's Phase 1 *might* migrate to SSO (Option A) or keep custom-JWT (Option B) — that decision is OUT OF SCOPE here. *(Constraint: don't presume the SSO migration; AdConnect MVP Phase 1 hasn't run yet.)*
+- **Standard routers (health, team, notificacoes) use Supabase auth via the seed framework** — `app/main.py` calls `create_product_app(..., standard_routers=["health", "notificacoes", "team"])`. These mount their own `make_get_current_user` from the seed factory (via `app/dependencies.py`'s `_db = create_database_module(settings, schema="adconnect")`). **Two auth realms coexist** in AdConnect — domain (custom JWT) + standard (Supabase). The Supabase realm is exercised by `tests/integration/test_e2e_flows.py:TestAuthBoundary`. *(Constraint: any change must preserve both realms.)*
+- **Don't touch the deprecated `ProductDependencies` class itself** — `seed/framework/backend/noctusai_seed/dependencies.py` already has the frame-aware DeprecationWarning (Phase 2 of `seed-auth-deps-hardening`, 2026-05-06). Cross-product rollout / deletion is a separate follow-up project. *(Constraint: stay in AdConnect's lane.)*
+- **Cross-cutting → root projects/** — slug = `auth-deps-shim-sweep`, lives at `projects/auth-deps-shim-sweep/`. Even though the only product touched is AdConnect, the project also rationalizes the canonical-pattern doc (KB) and may amend it. *(Per `KB § PATTERNS/project-execution.md §1 and §8`.)*
+- **Engineer commits per phase locally; pushes to `auth-deps-shim-sweep` branch at phase close** — never pushes to main. Final merge is the orchestrator's. *(Per the orchestrator role-split rule.)*
+
+---
+
+## 3. Design principles
+
+1. **Naming reflects the contract.** `auth_deps.py` named in the era before the seed-factory pattern existed; the file is fine but the *name* communicates "shim" / "leftover". Consider renaming to `app/jwt_auth.py` or `app/domain_auth.py` to make the realm explicit. **Decision deferred to Phase 1** — see §7 Open Questions.
+2. **Dead-code traps are debt, even when they pass tests.** `app/dependencies.py` re-exports the FastAPI-broken `ProductDependencies.get_org_id` / `get_user_role` / `get_user_client` — none of AdConnect's code uses them, but a future agent reading the file might wire them via `Depends(...)` and hit the 422 trap. Either delete the trap or scope down the export to the safe surface (admin/core/user clients).
+3. **Two-realm coexistence is OK; document it.** AdConnect's domain (custom JWT) + standard (Supabase) auth split is intentional and tested. The README / module docstrings should make this explicit so future readers don't try to "unify" them.
+4. **Tests over warnings as the safety net.** A keeper-detector that flags `Depends(<broken_method>)` (planned but not built) is the third defense layer. This project doesn't build the keeper, but it eliminates the *one product* that exposes the trap surface to FastAPI's solver.
+
